---
layout: "base.webc"
title: "2014 December"
id: "201412"
poemTitle: "Meaningful Christmas"
author: "Eila Webster"
endOfYear: false
---

<div class="full-width">
  <poem-grid class="wide" :title="poemTitle" :author="author" :theme="bgTheme">
    <!-- Header Section -->

    <poem-img
      src="/poems/meaningful_christmas_by_eila/image_5.png"
      alt=""
      slot="header-tl"
    ></poem-img>
    <poem-img
      src="/poems/meaningful_christmas_by_eila/image_6.png"
      alt=""
      slot="header-tr"
    ></poem-img>

    <!-- Column 1 Images (15%) -->
    <div slot="col-1-images"></div>

    <!-- Column 2 Text -->
    <div slot="col-2-text">
      <p>
        The old year’s ending and thoughts return <br />
        to the Christmas we knew long ago <br />
        Before commercial bodies took hold <br />
        With lavish gifts and tinsel show. <br />
        *****<br />
      </p>

      <p>
        Christmas held some meaning then <br />
        Singing Carols, hearts warmed by praise<br />
        Christmas greetings are no longer used <br />
        recently changed to Happy Holidays. <br />
        ***** <br />
      </p>

      <p>
        From late September in all the Stores<br />
        Christmas gifts glitter to catch the eye <br />
        As youngsters see the gadgets galore <br />
        that they want their kinfolk to buy. <br />
        *****
      </p>

      <p>
        It is like a competition for parents <br />
        All wanting the most expensive gift <br />
        Stretching and spending beyond means<br />
        Never giving a real thought to thrift <br />
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Column 3 Middle Images -->
    <div slot="col-3-images">
      <poem-img
        src="/poems/meaningful_christmas_by_eila/image_4.png"
        alt=""
      ></poem-img>
      <poem-img
        src="/poems/meaningful_christmas_by_eila/image_3.png"
        alt=""
      ></poem-img>
      <poem-img
        src="/poems/meaningful_christmas_by_eila/decs.png"
        style="border: none"
        alt=""
      ></poem-img>
      <poem-img
        src="/poems/meaningful_christmas_by_eila/manger.png"
        style="border: none"
        alt=""
      ></poem-img>
    </div>

    <!-- Column 4 Text -->
    <div slot="col-4-text">
      <p>
        Things then begin spinning out of control <br />
        New Year brings a real mess of debt<br />
        Trying to impress in this modern world <br />
        Can land you with lots of regret <br />
        ***** <br />
      </p>

      <p>
        What is wrong with a simple meal<br />
        A small gift picked from the tree <br />
        When generations joined in party games <br />
        the joy there, was plain to see <br />
        *****
      </p>

      <p>
        You can’t delete the Real Christmas <br />
        Nor the bright shining star in the sky <br />
        GOD keeps on sending us precious gifts <br />
        the ones that no money can buy.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Column 5 Images (15%) -->
    <div slot="col-5-images">
      <poem-img
        src="/poems/meaningful_christmas_by_eila/image.png"
        alt=""
      ></poem-img>
    </div>
  </poem-grid>
</div>
